WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
Speaker 1: Well, as we increasingly suspected,&nbsp;
the leak of the Supreme Court Roe v Wade decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:13.760
increasingly appears to have been leaked by&nbsp;
right wingers in order to ensure that Roe v&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.480
Wade was overturned. We have a new report from&nbsp;
Rolling Stone. It is absolutely fascinating and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:26.080
we are going to talk about it. But let me kind&nbsp;
of reset the story for you. When that decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.800
leaked, there was the immediate reaction&nbsp;
from the right that this was a left winger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.640
who leaked the decision to pressure justices&nbsp;
to vote to preserve Roe v Wade in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.720
intimidate them. And much of the reason for that&nbsp;
was that left wingers were rightly outraged that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.120
the Supreme Court planned to overturn Roe v Wade.&nbsp;
So the right said it was a left winger who did the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.960
leaking. We've got to investigate it. We've got&nbsp;
to figure out who it is. People should be fired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:01:00.080
disbarred, if they're lawyers, whatever. Now, I&nbsp;
took the approach of if we're just speculating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.680
could have been a left winger, could have&nbsp;
been a right winger. There were two scenarios.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:12.000
One potential scenario would be the leaker was on&nbsp;
the left, knew that the draft would overturn Roe v&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.800
Wade, and thought that by leaking it, it might&nbsp;
generate a pressure campaign to get a Supreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.400
Court justice or two to change their minds and&nbsp;
vote to preserve Roe v Wade. Just as plausibly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:28.880
the leaker could have been a right winger who&nbsp;
was aware that while this draft would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.440
overturned Roe v Wade, the February draft that&nbsp;
was leaked in, you know, a few months after that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.480
they may have known that within the court there&nbsp;
may have been justices changing their minds. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:47.440
the idea was to leak the draft, to publicize who,&nbsp;
as of February, planned to overturn Roe v Wade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.080
to make it difficult for them to change their&nbsp;
minds. These were the two speculative scenarios.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.640
And over time, as Republicans stop&nbsp;
talking about investigating the leaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.960
as we heard from longtime Supreme Court&nbsp;
reporters, that within the Supreme Court,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.880
the belief was actually that the leaker was a&nbsp;
right winger. I started to be of the mindset&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.080
that the leaker was probably a right winger. Well,&nbsp;
we now know from a new report that that appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:17.680
be correct. John Roberts was lobbying Kavanaugh&nbsp;
to save Roe. Then the draft opinion leaked. A new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.280
report says the leak, which conservatives insist&nbsp;
was the work of a rogue liberal, actually helped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:31.040
get Roe overturned. This was exactly the opinion&nbsp;
that I told you months ago was the most likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.760
immediately after the draft Supreme Court decision&nbsp;
was released. Conservatives began bleeding about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.400
how the leak was the work of a nefarious liberal&nbsp;
cleric who wanted to put the opinion out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.120
pressure the court's conservatives to change their&nbsp;
minds. It's possible that that's what happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.800
but if so, publicizing the draft had the opposite&nbsp;
effect, according to a new report from CNN. Per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.480
the report, the leak of the draft decision foiled&nbsp;
that Chief Justice Roberts attempts to persuade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:04.560
Brett Kavanaugh to act as Roe's saving vote.&nbsp;
Sources told CNN Roberts continued to try and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.040
sway the junior justices even after the leak of&nbsp;
the opinion, despite public and private pressure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.480
from conservatives for the court to solidify&nbsp;
its decision. Roberts overtures this spring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:20.080
particularly to Kavanaugh, raised fears among&nbsp;
conservatives and hopes among liberals that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.040
chief would change the outcome in the most closely&nbsp;
watched case in decades. Now, you might remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:32.960
Roberts ultimately voted to uphold the Mississippi&nbsp;
law. That was disputed, but he did a separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.520
concurrence disagreeing with the decision to&nbsp;
strike down Roe. So I know a lot of you might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:46.000
saying, but, David, the math doesn't work because&nbsp;
Roberts did vote to uphold Dobbs. And the belief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.040
is based on what he wrote and based on everything&nbsp;
that's being reported. Roberts wanted to uphold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.800
Dobbs, but still maintain Roe v Wade and&nbsp;
was working on Kavanaugh to do the same.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:04.560
This is exactly what it increasingly seemed like&nbsp;
within about eight or ten days of the leaked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:10.960
decision. And this thinking provides support&nbsp;
for the belief that the leaker was a right wing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.760
staffer. They wanted to prevent Brett Kavanaugh&nbsp;
from defecting. That's fundamentally what it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:23.360
and this is probably why we never heard it. How&nbsp;
is the search going for the real killer? O.J.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.120
what do we know? Right. It's the same type of&nbsp;
thing. We're going to investigate it. Oh, wait. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.120
was one of ours. Yeah, let's just never&nbsp;
mention that investigation again. And it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.880
very funny and also kind of disturbing how&nbsp;
in the days immediately following the leak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.680
everybody was saying the right wing&nbsp;
operatives were saying, what a travesty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.720
what a miscarriage of justice. This is criminal.&nbsp;
People need to be charged. People need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.520
disbarred. These left wingers leaking this stuff&nbsp;
and then we never hear about it again. And to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.600
perfectly frank, the dead giveaway was that&nbsp;
the right and conservative media went silent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.520
about the investigation and the leaker. About&nbsp;
a week or ten. Days after the leak took place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.800
Somebody maybe tipped them off and said,&nbsp;
don't even talk about this. The leaker was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.440
one of ours or not even just don't talk about&nbsp;
this. Don't say more about the investigation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.240
And that's what the report is. And it's exactly&nbsp;
what we and many of you believed at the time.

